<article class="env-lemma" id="017V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/017V">Lemma <span data-tag="017V">14.18.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $U$ be a simplicial object in $\mathcal{A}$. Then $U$ has a splitting obtained by taking $N(U_0) = U_0$ and for $m \geq 1$ taking </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  N(U_ m) = \bigcap \nolimits _{i = 0}^{m - 1} \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d^ m_ i).  \]
</div>
  <p> Moreover, this splitting is functorial on the category of simplicial objects of $\mathcal{A}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For any object $A$ of $\mathcal{A}$ we obtain a simplicial abelian group $\mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(A, U)$. Each of these are canonically split by Lemma <a href="/tag/017U" data-tag="017U">14.18.5</a>. Moreover, 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  N(\mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(A, U_ m)) = \bigcap \nolimits _{i = 0}^{m - 1} \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d^ m_ i) = \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(A, N(U_ m)).  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Hence we see that the morphism (<a href="/tag/017Q" data-tag="017Q">14.18.1.1</a>) becomes an isomorphism after applying the functor $\mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {A}(A, -)$ for any object of $\mathcal{A}$. Hence it is an isomorphism by the Yoneda lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>